      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Bumping this.  Add an option to lock the stretch value and only the stretch value.  The most in depth implementation would be to select what is locked when posed.  Stretch, position, rotation.\n\nRight now the only implementation I can think of is using a separate bone, parent constraints, and driving the parameters of the bone you want to stretch with the parameters of the control bone, but that's super unoptimized.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-08T23:35:56.148Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'd like to yank a rope and have it stretch and lock in place, but I would like to *not* lock it's rotation, so it resumes it's old pose but is now stretched, until the pose is released as normal and it returns to normal length.\n\nExample: Hoodie drawstrings that can be stretched, but continue to drape down when let go, just now longer.\n\nThis would be a new option under Posable in the Phys Bone script.",
